R3508 - the census and the entry index stop taking turns being red
==================================================================

Board head at open: R3508 item (0) - "census records index.html size/mtime/sha
while the entry index quotes the census byte counts", named as the one red gate
carrying a name. Criterion AC-PPC8 was pinned in src/os/backlog.md BEFORE any
code moved.

Read-only state at open
-----------------------
  python tools/preview_pair_census.py --check
    PPC-CHECK VERDICT FAIL read_only=True
      landed half is not this derivation: preview-pair-census.json
  python tools/deliverable_index.py --check
    VERDICT PASS 23/23 fingerprint=b158647b139c9908

  landed census json row for the index pair:
    html bytes=55908 sha=7BF86690 mtime=2026-11-26T09:35:53+08:00 verdict=no-json
  live preview/index.html: 55908 bytes sha=54B2EBE2
  -> same size, different bytes: the entry index had been re-derived after the
     census was written, and the census had recorded that re-derivation as a
     measurement of itself.

  preview/*.html naming this census page: exactly 1 (index.html), measured by
  scanning all 106 landed html halves for the label.

The change
----------
  tools/preview_pair_census.py
    + prints_this_page(path)   detection read off the landed html, not a list
    + mirror_row(stem, h, j)   class + last commit, no clock, no digest
    + census()                 a pair whose html half names this page is a
                               READING; every other pair keeps its measurements
    + html_of()                rows without a clock sort as 0 (mirror rows are
                               same-run or no-json, so they never list)
    + footer                   names the mirror rule and why it exists
  src/os/test_preview_pair_census.py
    + AC-PPC8                  4 sub-arms: detection set equality, no
                               measurement fields on mirror rows, narrowness on
                               every non-mirror row, negative control on
                               detection (a synthetic html that does not name
                               the page is refused), and negative control on the
                               reading (changing a mirror commit still reddens)
    ~ AC-PPC1                  REPAIR FOUND THIS WINDOW, recorded not folded in:
                               R3500 added the channel-receipt class but this
                               closure arm kept the R3499 tuple, so it counted
                               103 of 106 rows and had been red since R3500
                               without anyone re-running this suite. The
                               invariant is unchanged - one class per row, the
                               classes cover the tree - the tuple now names the
                               class that exists.
  src/sandbox/reconcile_all.py registry row preview-pair-census 7 -> 8

