Honest notes
------------
  (a) no landed page except the census pair and the entry index was re-derived;
      no freeze register, archive or AC-PPC1..7 threshold was touched; the
      index renderer was not changed at all - the fix is on the census side,
      which is one of the two roads the board named.
  (b) the exclusion is narrow by construction and pinned: every non-mirror row
      still records bytes/sha/mtime, and the mirror reading is still compared
      through its class and its commit.
  (c) the AC-PPC1 repair is a defect this window surfaced, not a threshold this
      window moved: the arm had been counting six classes while the tree had
      seven since R3500.
  (d) ZERO payment capability, no network beyond loopback; the five physical
      pieces still gate every buyer.

Second defect, found after the first export refresh
----------------------------------------------
  the census html half prints 'Tick 3507' and normalized() blanked the label only
  in the JSON branch, so the page went red the moment the tick advanced past its
  own derivation (measured: first difference at offset 1111, 'Tick 3507' vs
  'Tick 3508'). normalized() now blanks the tick label for html text too, and
  AC-PPC4 carries two new sub-arms: a rewritten tick is ignored, one changed count
  still reads drift.

Final gate order actually run: battery page -> census -> index -> export, then all
  three gates re-read green (PPC-CHECK PASS, AC-DIX 23/23, BSR-CHECK PASS, tick 3508).
